    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>As part of <strong>Convergence 2k26</strong>, the 27th National Level Annual Technical Symposium of VNR VJIET, the Software Hackathon provides a platform for students to apply their technical knowledge and innovative thinking towards solving contemporary real-world challenges.</p>\n<p>The hackathon is designed to encourage participants to develop practical and impactful solutions through collaboration, creativity and technology. Teams will work within a limited time frame to analyse problem statements, conceptualise solutions and develop functional prototypes. The event will be conducted offline at VNR VJIET, Hyderabad, on <strong>18th and 19th September</strong>, <strong>2026</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Domains:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fintech</li>\n<li>Procurement and Logistics</li>\n<li>Climate, Energy &amp; Green Technologies</li>\n<li>Healthcare Tech &amp; Wellness</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Process:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify a challenge from the problem statements provided across the respective domains.</li>\n<li>Build a practical and innovative solution by leveraging technologies of your choice.</li>\n<li>Prepare and submit the required deliverables according to the instructions and timeline provided.</li>\n<li>Entries will be reviewed and shortlisted based on their originality, feasibility, technical execution and potential for real-world application.</li>\n<li>Access the hackathon&nbsp;problem statements,&nbsp;guidelines,&nbsp;sample ppt template&nbsp;here.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Team Size:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>3 - 4 Members</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Duration:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>24 Hours (Offline)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Venue:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>E-Block, VNR VJIET, Hyderabad</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Highlights:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A competitive environment designed to encourage innovation.</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience in rapid solution development.</li>\n<li>Exposure to diverse technologies, ideas, and problem-solving approaches.</li>\n</ul>",
